{"uid":"4e34cac91997aba3","name":"test_the_second_ladder_flag_separates_unusable_findings_from_an_unreadable_verdict","fullName":"tests.test_contract_ladder#test_the_second_ladder_flag_separates_unusable_findings_from_an_unreadable_verdict","historyId":"959ff706383a5b198efef7a944b4fec9","time":{"start":1791915799098,"stop":1791915799139,"duration":41},"description":"Task 010 (requirement C.1, #219): `_review_contract_ladder` now\n    computes a SECOND flag (`self._review_findings_unusable`) alongside\n    `self._review_contract_unrepaired` -- one for a legible verdict claim\n    whose FINDINGS CHANNEL is what's unusable, the other for a verdict\n    claim that was never legible at all -- and `_review_verdict` reads\n    both (the new invariant assertions right where it already read the\n    first one).\n\n    Task 011 (requirement C.2, #219) gave the first flag its own pause\n    edge (`review_findings_unusable`), so scenario 1 below now lands on\n    the SAME kind of hold `review_contract_unrepaired` always has, rather\n    than the ordinary rejection ladder it rode under task 010 alone --\n    see `test_review_findings_unusable_pauses_and_never_archives_or_cures`\n    below for the full pause-shape assertions (state, pauseReason, no\n    approaches dir, approach counter, no cure pass) across the three\n    named unusable-findings shapes. This node keeps its original job: pin\n    that the two flags stay mutually exclusive and each fires only on its\n    own scenario -- an unreadable verdict claim still holds on\n    `review_contract_unrepaired`\n    (`test_ladder_exhaustion_holds_for_an_operator_and_never_archives`\n    above), never on the sibling edge.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 010 (requirement C.1, #219): <code>_review_contract_ladder</code> now<br />\ncomputes a SECOND flag (<code>self._review_findings_unusable</code>) alongside<br />\n<code>self._review_contract_unrepaired</code> -- one for a legible verdict claim<br />\nwhose FINDINGS CHANNEL is what's unusable, the other for a verdict<br />\nclaim that was never legible at all -- and <code>_review_verdict</code> reads<br />\nboth (the new invariant assertions right where it already read the<br />\nfirst one).</p>\n<pre><code>Task 011 (requirement C.2, #219) gave the first flag its own pause\nedge (`review_findings_unusable`), so scenario 1 below now lands on\nthe SAME kind of hold `review_contract_unrepaired` always has, rather\nthan the ordinary rejection ladder it rode under task 010 alone --\nsee `test_review_findings_unusable_pauses_and_never_archives_or_cures`\nbelow for the full pause-shape assertions (state, pauseReason, no\napproaches dir, approach counter, no cure pass) across the three\nnamed unusable-findings shapes. This node keeps its original job: pin\nthat the two flags stay mutually exclusive and each fires only on its\nown scenario -- an unreadable verdict claim still holds on\n`review_contract_unrepaired`\n(`test_ladder_exhaustion_holds_for_an_operator_and_never_archives`\nabove), never on the sibling edge.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791915518597,"stop":1791915518597,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791915518598,"stop":1791915518598,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791915799078,"stop":1791915799078,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name